ARTIFACTS ARE NOT COVERED BY THAT LICENSE

A steering vector is derived from model weights, so what may be done with one
is constrained by the license of the model its activations were read from, not
by the license on this code. The two are separate questions and this file keeps
them apart.

What this repository actually holds, as of 2026-09-19:

  artifacts/soham/d_olmo3_v1.safetensors
  artifacts/soham/d_olmo3_logistic.safetensors
  artifacts/soham/d_olmo3_lda.safetensors
  artifacts/soham/d_olmo3_L24_logistic.safetensors

      Directions derived from allenai/Olmo-3-1125-32B, which is Apache-2.0.
      Extracted by the author from github.com/soham-padia/steering-arena at
      commit b8b4721. See artifacts/REAL.md.

  fixtures/*.safetensors

      Synthetic. Integer ramps written by fixtures/build.py against model ids
      that resolve to nothing. Not derived from any model, and every number
      attached to them is invented and labeled as such. See
      fixtures/SYNTHETIC.md.

One artifact in the corpus is not in this repository:

  soham/meta-llama/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct/trauma@d61-diffmeans-expository-L34

      Derived from meta-llama/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct, which is the Llama 3.3
      Community License and is NOT Apache-2.0. Those bytes are published in
      the author's own Hugging Face namespace and this repository records only
      a pointer to them. Its row carries the author's dated reading of that
      license, including a clause he records as unresolved: whether the
      requirement to begin a derivative model's name with "Llama" reaches a
      read-out direction vector is not settled by the text.

The registry points at artifacts and serves none. A pointer is not a
redistribution, which is why the Llama-derived direction can be indexed here
while its bytes stay where their author put them.
